# L §4.2 (round 12): "the calendar a business-day function takes is a read of a calendar input, at any keys
# (cal[country[p]]); any other calendar expression (a def, an if) is refused (LOAD-UNIT)". (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED
# §4.2, writer 5's T-14.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input cal: calendar
def c2: calendar = cal
input d0: date
def d: date = add_business(d0, 1, c2)

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2026-01-01
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])
  d0 = 2026-03-02

ask q: d law 2026-03-02
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT add_business: its calendar c2 is not a read of a calendar input (m.tally:11)
